# Vibe-Wise Vault Sync

Syncs the vibe-wise learning files (`profile.md`, `project-map.md`, `progress.md`) between your
repos and a folder in your Obsidian vault, for people who work on more than one PC and want those
files to stay in sync.

## How it works

Each repo gets its own folder in the vault: `<vault>/<repo-name>/`. Git worktrees share the folder
of their main repo.

| When                                             | What happens                                           |
| ------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| You send `/vibe-wise:learn`                      | The session is marked as a learn session; vault → repo |
| A learn thread is reopened (resumed)             | vault → repo                                           |
| A learn session ends (settle, archive, or close) | repo → vault                                           |

Sessions that never ran `/vibe-wise:learn` never push, so an outdated local copy can't overwrite
newer state in the vault.

Under the hood, it's three hooks (`UserPromptSubmit`, `SessionStart` with the `resume`
matcher, and `SessionEnd`) that call `vibe-wise-sync.sh`. Every sync is logged to
`~/.claude/vibe-wise-sync/sync.log`.

## Requirements

- Claude Code with the [vibe-wise](https://github.com/nykooi1/vibe-wise) plugin
- `git`, `rsync`, and `python3`
- Linux, macOS, or WSL (the script is bash; native Windows isn't supported)

## Install

Send this prompt to your agent, replacing `{VAULT_PATH}` with the folder where the files should
be stored:

```
Install the hook from https://github.com/gustavo-zorzo/vibe-wise-vault-sync following its README.
The vault path is: {VAULT_PATH}
```

Or install it manually:

1. Copy `vibe-wise-sync.sh` to `~/.claude/hooks/` and make it executable:
   `chmod +x ~/.claude/hooks/vibe-wise-sync.sh`
2. **Merge** these hooks into `~/.claude/settings.json`. Don't replace the file; keep any hooks
   you already have:

   ```json
   "hooks": {
     "UserPromptSubmit": [
       { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "timeout": 30,
         "command": "VIBE_WISE_VAULT='{VAULT_PATH}' \"$HOME/.claude/hooks/vibe-wise-sync.sh\" pull" }] }
     ],
     "SessionStart": [
       { "matcher": "resume", "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "timeout": 30,
         "command": "VIBE_WISE_VAULT='{VAULT_PATH}' \"$HOME/.claude/hooks/vibe-wise-sync.sh\" resume" }] }
     ],
     "SessionEnd": [
       { "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "timeout": 30,
         "command": "VIBE_WISE_VAULT='{VAULT_PATH}' \"$HOME/.claude/hooks/vibe-wise-sync.sh\" push" }] }
     ]
   }
   ```

Hooks only apply to sessions started after the install. Repeat these steps on every PC, each with
its own vault path.

### Vault path format

Use the path as the shell running Claude Code sees it. On WSL, a Windows path like
`G:\Meu Drive\Vault\Vibe Wise` becomes `/mnt/g/Meu Drive/Vault/Vibe Wise`.

WSL only mounts physical drives automatically. Virtual drives, such as the one Google Drive for
desktop creates, have to be mounted by hand:

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/g
sudo mount -t drvfs G: /mnt/g
echo 'G: /mnt/g drvfs defaults 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab   # mount it on every boot
```

If the vault path isn't reachable (drive not mounted, Google Drive not running yet), the hook
logs it and skips the sync. It never blocks your prompt.

## Limitations

- **Never use two PCs at the same time.** The last push wins and overwrites the other PC's progress.
- **After switching PCs, wait for your cloud drive to finish syncing** before running
  `/vibe-wise:learn`; otherwise you'll pull an outdated copy.
- **If Claude Code is killed or crashes,** `SessionEnd` may not run. That session's changes then
  stay only on that PC and can be overwritten by the next pull.
- **Files are copied, never deleted.** A file removed on one side stays on the other.
- Files are compared by content (`rsync -c`), because Google Drive doesn't allow setting file
  modification times.
- `project-map.md` describes the architecture of the repo you're working on. Check your company's
  policy before syncing work repos to a personal drive.

## Roadmap

- A single `profile.md` shared across all projects, instead of one copy per project folder.
